# CODEOWNERS — platform chart ownership
#
# NOTE (sandbox, 2026-10-03): only one real account exists in this org
# (@pseudonative), so every pattern below currently maps to the same
# owner — demonstrating the correct ownership STRUCTURE, not enforcing
# real review (require_code_owner_reviews is deliberately left OFF in
# branch protection; see e7n-791-mini-explainers.txt entry for why).
# In a real multi-person org, replace these with actual GitHub teams
# (e.g. @org/platform-team, @org/network-team) matched to who genuinely
# owns each area, then turn enforcement on.
#
# Last-matching pattern wins, same as .gitignore. Most specific patterns
# go at the bottom.

# Default owner for anything not matched below
*                             @pseudonative

# The publish pipeline itself — changes here affect EVERY chart's
# publish path, not just one. Should always require review regardless
# of which chart directory a PR also touches.
/.github/workflows/          @pseudonative
/.github/scripts/            @pseudonative
/test/bats/                  @pseudonative

# Chart directories, by area
/network/                    @pseudonative
/cloud/                      @pseudonative
/shared/                     @pseudonative
/poc/                        @pseudonative
